TI-99/4A core: the machine is zeldin/Mega99 (https://github.com/zeldin/Mega99), vendored from commit 82ce2157f62688eb0cd58332b52eba0eeed77538.
Licence: LGPL-3.0 (LICENSE-Mega99.txt in rtl/src); the files carry their own headers, listed below as found (first licence line of each file).
Not vendored: the board level files (tops, clock wizards, HyperRAM, MIG, QSPI, ICAP, the OpenRISC service processor and its MMIO, keyboard/PS2 front ends,
TMDS/audio DACs) and clkgen.v, which rtl/trx/clkgen_nco.v replaces (a phase accumulator per clock enable that follows the host's System Mode, with a hold input).
No ROM is part of this repository: the console ROM and the GROMs come from the person's stick (MAME ti99_4a set names).

Changes against upstream (full diff: rtl/mega99-trims.patch):
  mainboard.v   parameters INCLUDE_VSP, INCLUDE_TIPI, NUM_GROMS; ports clk_mode and clk_hold (to the replacement clkgen)
  peb.v         parameter INCLUDE_TIPI (generate wrapper with tie-offs)
  grom_storage_bram.v   per GROM and 2K page arrays so that NUM_GROMS cuts block RAM (equivalent behaviour, checked by simulation)

